  "note": "The common lizard (doc 13, The year, season by season: summer; docs/future/11 finds): basks flat on a sunny stone on dry ground, more often among the gorse. A find: nothing saved, no needs, no gift (src/world/creatures/sun-finds.js, live). WHEN: in the seasons listed (late spring counts from springFrom of the way through spring), between hours[0] and hours[1] o'clock, on days whose weather is one of moods. WHERE: on a stone you set or that came by itself (the pieces' seats, kind stone, out of the water), on each with chance a day, or gorseChance with gorse growing within gorseM; seeded by the stone and the day. LOOK: a blended-SDF lizard in real meters (about 12 cm with its tail), drawn at displayScale 2.5 (Matt's rescale rule for small lives): brown back with a dark mid-line and pale flank lines, splayed legs, a long tapering tail curled to one side. RIG (LZ): 14 bones (body, head, each leg in two parts, four tail segments), posed by src/world/creatures/rigs/lizard.js and lived by src/world/creatures/lizard-live.js: a low sprawl with toes spread and the tail curled to a side (curlDeg), flanks breathing (breathS), the head lifting and turning in quick small jerks (jerkEveryS, snapped at jerkHz), a few push-up bobs now and then (pushEveryS); when you come within presence.ringM (calmShare of it if you come slowly) or edit beside it it darts off the stone away from you (dartMps, dartM), waits low (hideS) and comes back in short bursts (burstS, pauseS), legs sweeping in diagonal pairs with the spine and tail waving (gait).",
